# Secrets for this agent. Never commit real values.
#
# The gateway reads this file at its own HERMES_HOME/.env through the home
# mount -- compose passes no credentials. That is the whole contract for
# PLOW_HOME_CHANNEL.
#
# The Plow credential itself is NOT here: `agent-mgr activate` mints it into
# a file OUTSIDE every agent's home (`agent-mgr resolve` never prints it),
# because the gateway strips those keys out of this file on every boot.

# Written in place by `agent-mgr set-home`; do not fill it by hand.
PLOW_HOME_CHANNEL=

# Plow Latch: which Mac this agent drives, and its relay credential. Mint both
# from the Mac running Plow Latch, then `agent-mgr set-latch atlas-agent`,
# which reads them on stdin and writes them here, so the token never reaches a
# shell history or the process table. `KEY=value` at column 0 is the form
# agent-mgr writes and the only one it reads back.
#
# Shipped bare, with no `=`: a PRESENT key with a blank value still clobbers a
# credential the container's own environment supplies, because hermes' dotenv
# load keys off presence, not emptiness. A bare line reads as absent instead.
DOMO_DEVICE_UID
DOMO_MCP_TOKEN

# Which model plow-init writes into config.yaml at every boot. config.yaml's
# own model: block is NOT authoritative for this image -- plow-init
# (/etc/s6-overlay/scripts/plow-init.py) rewrites model.provider/model.default
# from these two on every boot, defaulting to the Plow-hosted model when
# either is unset (confirmed live: model.default kept resetting to
# anthropic/claude-sonnet-5 under provider: plow no matter what config.yaml
# declared, until these were set). Also register the matching key with
# `hermes auth add <provider> --type api-key` -- these two name which
# provider/model to use, not the credential to use it with.
HERMES_PROVIDER=openrouter
HERMES_MODEL=google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite
